<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vasudeva Kanva</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 73–64 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasudeva">Vasudeva</a> Kanva was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmin</a> minister who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanva-dynasty">Kanva dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magadha">Magadha</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> around 73 BCE. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puranas">Puranas</a> and the writer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banabhatta">Bana</a>, he had his master <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/devabhuti">Devabhuti</a>, the last king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shunga-empire">Shunga dynasty</a>, killed and took the throne. His dynasty of four kings ruled for about 45 years.</p></div>
